data/shops/
_delete_me_test_artifacts/

# Agent working memory. The directory is volatile scratch and stays ignored,
# with ONE exception: STATUS.md is tracked, because the global process requires
# a fresh session to read it before starting work and an untracked file cannot
# serve that purpose for anyone but the machine it happens to sit on.
# A negation cannot re-include a file under an excluded DIRECTORY, which is why
# this ignores the contents (.agents/*) rather than the directory itself.
# Committed specs and plans still live in docs/, not here.
.agents/*
!.agents/STATUS.md
!.agents/ARCHIVE.md

# Vite bundle - rebuilt from src/ on every deploy, never committed.
public/dist/

# public/r/ (the built shadcn registry) is deliberately NOT ignored. The CI
# drift gate diffs a fresh `shadcn build` against the committed output to
# catch hand-edited components; with nothing committed there is nothing to
# diff and the gate passes vacuously.

# Workshop job attachments and uploaded images. A named Docker volume in
# production (docker-compose.yml); a real directory here when the server runs
# on the host, including during tests. Customer files must never be
# committable.
uploads/
